    "created_at": "2017-03-21T15:54:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-21T15:54:16Z",
    "body": "I came up with\r\n```\r\n<p><dfn><code>about:blank</code></dfn> is a <a for=/>URL</a> whose <a for=url>scheme</a> is\r\n\"<code>about</code>\", <a for=url>path</a> is « \"<code>blank</code>\" », and\r\n<a for=url>cannot-be-a-base-URL flag</a> is set.\r\n```\r\nbut then I realized that when we compare about:blank we ignore most components (not all implementations do though) so this wouldn't be exactly correct either. Defining it as the result of parsing or some such wouldn't account for that either.",
