    "created_at": "2017-03-24T04:39:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-24T04:39:22Z",
    "body": "Hmm, I was thinking the definition would be a simple one like those at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#about:legacy-compat and friends. Maybe there is a more general issue with comparing with about: URLs?\r\n\r\nHere are the parts of the spec where we compare with about:blank:\r\n\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-object-element:about:blank\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-object-element:about:blank-2\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#apis-for-creating-and-navigating-browsing-contexts-by-name:about:blank-4\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#origin:about:blank-3 , sorta?\r\n\r\nMost of the other references to this term are actually talking about the \"about:blank Document\" and so aren't affected by the concerns you mention.\r\n\r\nMy suggestion would be to write web platform tests for these cases and see if we have a majority browser behavior. If they don't treat `about:blank?foo#bar`, or `about:blank#bar` as `about:blank` for the purposes of those 3-4 spec parts, then your proposal in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/816#issuecomment-288124345 is fine as-is. If they do, then we need to introduce a new term, in addition to about:blank, such as \"equivalent to about:blank\", or maybe even something general for comparing URLs without query and fragment.\r\n\r\nI guess this ends up being more work than the simple \"add a definition\" the bug looks like. I'd be fine splitting this into a new bug for URL comparison and just adding a definition like we have for about:legacy-compat to close out this bug.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
